@startuml buffer-page-lifecycle-2
' ============================================================================
' Buffer-pool PAGE (frame) lifecycle, PART 2 of 2 — the RESIDENT composite's
' internal substates: the product {clean, dirty} × {pinned, unpinned} that a
' page cycles through while it occupies a buffer-pool frame, and the operations
' that move it between them. The enclosing Disk ⇄ Resident ⇄ eviction cycle is
' the companion figure buffer-page-lifecycle.puml (PART 1).
'
' Source of truth: src/persistent_artrie/core/buffer_manager.rs
'   A `Frame` carries  block_id · lease_state (read-pin count | WRITE_LEASE) ·
'   dirty flag · reference_bit (CLOCK second-chance).
'   Operations:  pin_read / pin_write · unpin_read / unpin_write ·
'   mark_dirty (on write) · flush_page / flush_all (write-back → clear_dirty).
'   Invariants enforced by the code:
'     · a frame is NOT evictable while pinned (any read lease or the write lease);
'     · a dirty frame may NOT be flushed while a WRITE_LEASE is held;
'     · the CLOCK victim must be unpinned AND have reference_bit == 0;
'     · a dirty victim is written back (clear_dirty) before its frame is reused.
'
' Color key:
'   green (#C8E6C9) = page is RESIDENT in a buffer-pool frame (in memory)
'   red   (#C62828) = the write-transition (mark_dirty under a WRITE_LEASE)
'   grey  (#ECEFF1) = infrastructure note
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 210
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}

title Resident (buffer-pool frame) — internal substates (2 of 2)\nClean/Dirty × Pinned/Unpinned

state "Resident (buffer-pool frame)" as Resident #C8E6C9 {

  state "Clean · Unpinned" as CleanUnpinned #C8E6C9 : dirty=false · lease=0\n→ CLOCK-evictable
  state "Clean · Pinned" as CleanPinned #C8E6C9 : read/write lease held\n→ pinned, NOT evictable
  state "Dirty · Pinned" as DirtyPinned #C8E6C9 : modified under a lease\n(differs from disk)
  state "Dirty · Unpinned" as DirtyUnpinned #C8E6C9 : modified · leases dropped\n→ flush before reuse

  [*] --> CleanUnpinned : entry\n(fault-in populates)

  CleanUnpinned --> CleanPinned : pin_read / pin_write
  CleanPinned --> CleanUnpinned : unpin (no writes)

  CleanPinned -[#C62828]-> DirtyPinned : mark_dirty\n(under WRITE_LEASE)
  DirtyPinned --> DirtyUnpinned : unpin_write\n(still dirty)

  DirtyUnpinned --> CleanUnpinned : flush_page / flush_all\n→ clear_dirty
  DirtyPinned --> DirtyPinned : flush blocked\n(WRITE_LEASE held)
}

note bottom of Resident #ECEFF1
  Entry from **fault-in** (PART 1) populates **Clean · Unpinned**.
  Eviction (PART 1) leaves the frame from **Clean · Unpinned**
  (clean → reuse as-is) or **Dirty · Unpinned** (write-back →
  clear_dirty), so no acknowledged bytes are lost.
end note

legend right
| Color | Page condition |
|<#C8E6C9>| resident in a buffer-pool frame |
|<#C62828>| write-transition (mark_dirty) |
endlegend
@enduml
